      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT to understand the code before improving understandability.Now I understand the test: it verifies that when the threshold is `0`, comparing an empty string against a 16-character string returns `-1` (distance exceeds threshold). Let me write an improved version with clearer naming and intent.The improved test compiles successfully. The refactored version uses descriptive variable names (`threshold`, `distanceWithZeroThreshold`, `emptySource`, `nonEmptyTarget`, `result`) and adds a comment explaining why the expected result is `-1`."
